From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] boringssl: build static so symbols link into adb

Buildroot configures CMake with -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON, so the vendored
BoringSSL builds libcrypto.so/libssl.so. Those .so files are NOT installed
to the target rootfs (only the adb binary is), and adb's RPATH points at
the build tree. On the device the dynamic linker therefore resolves
libcrypto.so/libssl.so to the rootfs OpenSSL 1.1.1, which lacks the
BoringSSL-only symbols adb needs, and adb aborts at startup:

  /usr/bin/adb: symbol 'SPAKE2_CTX_new': can't resolve symbol
  /usr/bin/adb: symbol 'EVP_AEAD_CTX_init': can't resolve symbol
  ... (SPAKE2, EVP_AEAD, CRYPTO_BUFFER, sk_*, HKDF, etc.)

Force BoringSSL to build as static libraries (with position-independent
code, since adb is a PIE) by toggling BUILD_SHARED_LIBS off only around
its add_subdirectory. Its symbols then link directly into the adb binary,
and the external shared deps (protobuf, brotli, lz4, usb, z, zstd), which
ARE installed to the rootfs, remain dynamically linked.

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
---
--- a/vendor/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/vendor/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,7 +1,16 @@
 # TODO: https://cmake.org/cmake/help/v3.0/module/ExternalProject.html
 # To patch the submodule
 
+# Aiden: force BoringSSL to build as STATIC libs (with PIC) so its
+# symbols are baked into the adb PIE binary. Buildroot sets
+# BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON globally, which would otherwise produce
+# libcrypto.so/libssl.so that are never installed to the rootfs,
+# leaving adb to pick up the rootfs OpenSSL (missing BoringSSL syms).
+set(_aiden_saved_shared ${BUILD_SHARED_LIBS})
+set(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS OFF)
+set(CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON)
 add_subdirectory(boringssl EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL)
+set(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS ${_aiden_saved_shared})
 set(android-vendored
 	avb
 	base
